          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              \-rig
            is supposed to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            of that of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
          %p
            Just as a rig is a multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            whose underlying set also has a notion of addition, so a
            = succeed "-rig" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            whose underlying category also has a notion of addition, and we can describe this notion of addition in a few different ways.
          %p
            Note that we don't expect a
            = succeed "-rig" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg+swindle"} Eilenberg swindle
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          %p
            Compare also the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig+category"} rig category
          %h2#Definitions Definitions
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            involves some arbitrary choices that will be determined by the precise intended application, there is a bit of flexibility of what exactly one may want to call a
            = succeed "." do
              %em 2-ring
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#EnrichedMonoidalCategories"} Enriched monoidal categories
          %p
            But a central aspect of an ordinary ring is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+law"} distributivity law
            which says that the product in the ring preserves sums. Since sums in a 2-ring are given by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            in that the the tensor product preserves colimits:
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#MonoidalCompleteCateories"} Compatibly monoidal cocomplete categories
          %p
            But there are still more properties which one may want to enforce, notably that homomorphisms of 2-rings form a
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                2-abelian group
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/2-abelian+group"} ?
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+category"} presentable
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#CompatiblyMonoidalPresentableCategories"}> Compatibly monoidal presentable categories
              \.
          %h3#EnrichedMonoidalCategories Enriched monoidal categories
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                  \-rig
                might be an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+category"} Ab-enriched category
                which is
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    enriched monoidal
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/enriched+monoidal+category"} ?
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                  \-rig
                might be an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
                which is enriched monoidal.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                  \-rig
                might be a
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+monoidal+category"} distributive monoidal category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                such that the monoidal product distributes over the coproducts.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                  \-rig
                might be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
                with finite coproducts.
            %li
              %p
                Finally, a
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                  \-ring
                is a monoidal
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          %p
            Note that (2) is a special case of both (1) and (3), which are independent. (4) is a special case of (3), by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
          %h3#MonoidalCompleteCateories Compatibly monoidal cocomplete categories
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#BaezDolan"}> Baez-Dolan
            ) the following is considered:
          #BD2Rig.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %em 2-rig
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} cocomplete category
              where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              respects
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
          %p
            One can define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            2-rigs in this sense (and indeed, also in the other senses listed above). In particular, there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mrow
                      %mi Symm
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Rig
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Symm2Rig}
            with:
          %ul
            %li
              %p symmetric monoidal cocomplete categories where the monoidal product distributes over colimits as objects,
            %li
              %p symmetric monoidal cocontinuous functors as 1-morphisms,
            %li
              %p symmetric monoidal natural transformations as 2-morphisms.
          %h3#CompatiblyMonoidalPresentableCategories Compatibly monoidal presentable categories
          %p
            The following refines the
            %a{:href => "#MonoidalCompleteCateories"} above
            by demanding the underlying category of a 2-ring to be not just cocomplete but even a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+category"} presentable category
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#CJF"} CJF, remark 2.1.10
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    2 Ab \in 2Cat
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+categories"} presentable categories
              and
              = succeed "-preserving" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              between them.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CJF"}> CJF, def. 2.1.8
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              By the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
              this is equivalently the 2-category of presentable categories and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              functors between them.
          #CategoryOfModulesAs2AbelianGroup.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Given an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              is presentable, hence may be regarded as a 2-abelian group.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CJF"}> CJF, example 2.1.5
            )
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Ab
              is a
              %span.newWikiWord
                closed
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/closed+monoidal+2-category"} ?
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+2-category"} symmetric monoidal 2-category
              with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊠
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo ×
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \boxtimes \colon 2Ab \times 2Ab \to 2Ab
              such that for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo ∈
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B, C \in 2Ab
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊠
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{2Ab}(A \boxtimes B, C)
              is equivalently the full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{Cat}(A \times B, C)
              on those that are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+function"} bilinear
              in that they preserve
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              in each argument separately.
          %p
            See also at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pr%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} Pr(∞,1)Cat
            for more on this.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\mathcal{C}}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+category"} presentable
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ⊠
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Set^{\mathcal{C}_1} \boxtimes
                    Set^{\mathcal{C}_2}
                    \\simeq
                    Set^{\mathcal{C}_1 \times \mathcal{C}_2}
                    \\,.
          #TensorProductModuleCategoriesAsOf2AbelianGroups.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              is presentable and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ⊠
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Mod_{R_1} \boxtimes Mod_{R_2}
                    \\simeq
                    Mod_{R_1 \otimes R_2}
                    \\,,
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CJF"}> CJF, example 2.2.7
            )
          #EilenbergWattsTheorem.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi R
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_1, R_2
              two rings, the category of 2-abelian group homomorphisms between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+modules"} categories of modules
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalence"} naturally equivalent
              to that of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_1
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodules"} bimodules
              and their
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intertwiners"} intertwiners
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)\otimes (-)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    {}_{R_1}Mod_{R_2}
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    Hom_{2Ab}(Mod_{R_1}, Mod_{R_2})
                    \\,.
            %p
              The equivalence sends a bimodule
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              to the functor given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              over
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi N
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi R
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-) \otimes N \;\colon\;
                    Mod_{R_1} \to Mod_{R_2}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Watts+theorem"} Eilenberg-Watts theorem
          #2RingAsCompatiblyMonoidalPresentableCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Ring
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    2Ring \in 2Cat
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+objects"} monoid objects
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 Ab
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              of this 2-category we call a
              = succeed "." do
                %strong 2-ring
            %p
              Equivalently, a 2-ring in this sense is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+category"} presentable category
              equipped with the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              where the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              preserves
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CJF"}> CJF, def. 2.1.8
            )
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              with its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
              is a 2-ring and it is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Ring
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Ring
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CJF"}> CJF, example 2.3.4
            )
          .num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              with its standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              is a 2-ring.
          #CommutativeRingGivesCommutative2Ring.num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              an ordinary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              equipped with its usual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
              is a commutative 2-ring.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_7 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              its ordinary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfModulesAs2AbelianGroup"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              is equivalently the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sesquiunital+sesquialgebra"} sesquiunital sesquialgebra
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is in addition a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              is a commutative 2-ring and is canonically an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-algebra"} 2-algebra
              in that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ab \simeq Mod_{\mathbb{Z}} \to Mod_R
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CJF"}> CJF, example 2.3.7
            )
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a 2-ring, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#2RingAsCompatiblyMonoidalPresentableCategory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mn 2
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    2Mod_A \in 2Cat
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+objects"} module objects
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Ab
            %p
              This means that a 2-module over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+category"} presentable category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              equipped with a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊠
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \boxtimes N \to N
            %p which satisfies the evident action property.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#CJF"}> CJF, def. 2.3.3
            )
          .num_example
            %h6#example_8 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              be an ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              an ordinary
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfModulesAs2AbelianGroup"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_A
              is a 2-abelian group and by example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CommutativeRingGivesCommutative2Ring"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              is a commutative ring. By example
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TensorProductModuleCategoriesAsOf2AbelianGroups"}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-module"} 2-module
              structures on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi R
                    %mo ⊠
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Mod
                      %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Mod_R \boxtimes \Mod_A \to Mod_A
            %p correspond to colimit-preserving functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi ℤ
                        %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Mod_{R \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} A} \to Mod_{A}
            %p
              that satisfy the action property. Such as presented under the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Watts+theorem"} Eilenberg-Watts theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EilenbergWattsTheorem"}
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℤ
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodules"} bimodules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              itself is canonically such a bimodule and it exhibits a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-module"} 2-module
              structure on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_A
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#PropertiesInitialObject Initial object
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The analog role in 2-rigs to the role played by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              among ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigs"} rigs
              should be played by the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
              of the natural numbers: the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+finite+sets"} category of finite sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FinSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FinSet
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              (in the suitably higher categorical sense) in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of 2-rigs.
            %p
              For the notion in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BD2Rig"}
              this was conjectured by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"} John Baez
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#2RingAsCompatiblyMonoidalPresentableCategory"}
              this is asserted in (
              %a{:href => "#CJF"}> Chirvasitu &amp; Johnson-Freyd, example 2.3.4
              ).
